From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H96 build <builder@h96-build>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] drm/bridge: dw-hdmi-qp: fix audio infoframe pack error
 check

hdmi_audio_infoframe_pack() returns the packed length or a negative
error; dw_hdmi_qp_set_audio_infoframe() tested if (!ret) and so
treated success as failure. Test ret < 0, as upstream already does in
dw_hdmi_qp_init_audio_infoframe().

H96 series: 0f8ff828b / 62e17b046.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
index 076d3ea73..213814329 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-hdmi-qp.c
@@ -958,7 +958,7 @@ void dw_hdmi_qp_set_audio_infoframe(struct dw_hdmi_qp *hdmi,
 
 	ret = hdmi_audio_infoframe_pack(&hparms->cea, infoframe_buf,
 					sizeof(infoframe_buf));
-	if (!ret) {
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_err(hdmi->dev, "%s: Failed to pack audio infoframe: %d\n",
 			__func__, ret);
 		return;
